<!--
  Hub home — the primary app's index route (`/`).

  The simplest possible page: a heading and a subheading. No chrome,
  no controller, no state. The point is to prove the route renders
  and the framework + bundler agree on the path. Real chrome and
  data come in follow-up commits — port the shell's `sui-nav-top`,
  `sui-status-bar`, `sui-command-bar` (one at a time, accepting the
  `window.ship` breakage, fixing in subsequent commits) and let
  this page grow its launch surface.
-->
<main>
  <h1>Hub</h1>
  <p>Ship's primary app — ready when you are.</p>
</main>
